  "_meta": {
    "fixture_name": "vi-grammar-cases",
    "schema_version": 1,
    "purpose": "Held-out Vietnamese-learner grammar error cases for the L1 detector eval harness. Seeded from the C1 taxonomy at docs/l1-taxonomies/vi-grammar.md plus a handful of detector-candidate gap markers for vi_l1_subject_gender, vi_l1_topic_comment_fronting, vi_l1_co_transfer, and vi_l1_future_adverb_bare (none of which have rules yet).",
    "source_notes": [
      "Sentence phrasing drawn from public/data/english_a1_*.json and english_b1_*.json corpus textures (I am from Vietnam, She has long hair, etc.), then mutated to introduce a single L1-transfer error.",
      "expected_category semantics — expected_pass: detector should fire AND tag matches expected_rule_id; expected_partial: detector should fire ANY tag (parent/related); expected_failure: detector should NOT fire (case documents a gap for a detector candidate). expected_failure cases are excluded from the baseline pass-rate denominator.",
      "When a new detector ships (e.g. vi_l1_topic_comment_fronting), flip the relevant expected_failure cases to expected_pass and re-run with --update-baseline.",
      "C1-taxonomy provenance points at docs/l1-taxonomies/vi-grammar.md sections 1–15.",
      "ALL CASE IDs are stable. Do not renumber when adding new cases — append."
    ]
  },
